{title: I Will Sing the Wondrous Story}
{artist: Francis H. Rowley / Peter P. Bilhorn}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 94}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Tabernacle Hymns Number Three (Chicago, llinois: Tabernacle Publishing, 1950), # 105)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]I will sing the wondrous story
[D]Of the [A7]Christ who died for [D]me.
[D]How He left His home in glory
[D]For the [A7]cross of Calva[D]ry.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Yes, I’ll sing the [A]wondrous sto__[D]__ry
[D]Of the [A7]Christ who [G]died for [D]me,
[D]Sing it with the saints in glory,
[D]Ga__[F#m]__thered by__[A7]__ the crystal sea.__[D]__
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]I was lost, but Jesus found me,
[D]Found the [A7]sheep that went a[D]stray,
[D]Threw His loving arms around me,
[D]Drew me [A7]back into His [D]way.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]I was bruised, but Jesus healed me,
[D]Faint was [A7]I from many a [D]fall,
[D]Sight was gone, and fears possessed me,
[D]But He [A7]freed me from them [D]all.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Days of darkness still come o’er me,
[D]Sorrow’s [A7]path I often [D]tread,
[D]But the Savior still is with me;
[D]By His [A7]hand I’m safely [D]led.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]He will keep me till the river
[D]Rolls its [A7]waters at my [D]feet;
[D]Then He’ll bear me safely over,
[D]Where the [A7]loved ones I shall [D]meet.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
